{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed floorspace for the first floor flat falls below the minimum Gross Internal Area (GIA) standards required for a three-bedroom (five-person) unit. In addition to the undersized bedroom and living/kitchen/dining areas, the layout results in a substandard and cramped form of accommodation that would be detrimental to the living conditions of future occupiers. Furthermore, the flat offers a poor outlook from the living room and includes only a single shower room, which is inadequate for a family-sized unit. Taken together, these deficiencies contribute to an unacceptable standard of residential accommodation. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D3 D (7) and (11) and D6 of the London Plan (2021); Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013); the London Plan Guidance: Housing Design Standards (2023); and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
